@startuml direct-rialto-preroll-monitor-state
title AampRialtoPreRollMonitor states (epoch discards abandoned polls)

[*] --> Idle

Idle --> Polling : Start(probe)\n[stop old timer, ++epoch,\nrecord start time, schedule 10 ms timer]
Idle --> Completed : Start(probe)\n[timer could not be scheduled:\ncomplete immediately]

state Polling {
  [*] --> Evaluate
  Evaluate : copy probe, epoch, start (under mutex)
  Evaluate : evaluate probes without the mutex
  Evaluate --> Evaluate : no reason yet\n[log only if frame count changed]
}

Polling --> Completed : reason found and epoch unchanged\n(target reached > buffer full >\nend of stream > timeout)
Polling --> Idle : Stop()\n[++epoch, stop timer (waits for a running\nPoll), release probe]
Polling --> Polling : Start(probe) again\n[restart with new epoch]

Completed --> Idle : release probe;\nrun completion action without the mutex
Completed : log "pre-roll complete (<reason>) after N ms"

note right of Polling
  A Poll whose copied epoch no longer
  matches (Stop or restart happened
  meanwhile) stops silently and
  never completes.
end note
@enduml
